{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1345679-soul-pacts-and-pact-benefits","id":1345679,"title":"Soul Pacts and Pact Benefits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-03T18:01:03-08:00","id":1345679,"title":"Soul Pacts and Pact Benefits","content":"Question: When a demon calls in a Soul Pact, do they retain any benefits the signer may have negotiated for? I mean, suppose a mortal sold his soul for wealth or supernatural skill as a musician' would the demon then &quot;inherit&quot; the wealth/skill bonus when they took over the mortal's identity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T18:36:17-08:00","id":1345684,"title":"","content":"I'd say they do, the book states that a lot of Demons sign Soul Pacts with mortals, but delay the moment of cashing in the Pact and taking that mortal as a Cover, because they manipulate the mortal into living a life that will eventually be more confortable for the Demon once they finally cash in the Pact. A demon could convince a person in a very desperate situation to sign their Soul away and keep aking that person's life better and better for when he takes that life for himself and the mortal would never think about the Demon's nefarious reasons for that.<br /> <br /> So yeah, as an ST I'd relu that if the benefit the mortal won with the Pact was properly incorporated into that person's life, there's no reason the Demon shouldn't have access to it once he cashes the Pact in. You could represent that with bonus or merits that are only accessible to that Cover if you don't feel like those benefits would incorporate well into the Demon's own Primum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T15:36:40-08:00","id":1345924,"title":"","content":"I think the answer is kind of:<br /> <br /> So they definitely don't get the merits added onto their character sheet upon taking on that cover, because that isn't mechanically how it works in general. Skills and Merits the cover would have that the demon doesn't can be accessed by Legend (and it also gives a good reason to buy these merits in game.) If merits transferred with cover you wouldn't need that system at all. Also there will be below the abstraction layer quality of life stuff. <br /> <br /> Personally I would rule that it needed to have been conceptually bedded in to a degree, if you sign a riches for soul pact with Jillian who is crashing on her friends couch because she can't get a deposit together. That money isn't really part of how people see her, and you don't have the idea of Jillian's affluence to use with Legend. On the other hand if you leave it a few months that sudden influx of resource will have changed the nature of the cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/711-mcgonigle","name":"mcgonigle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}